{"kind":"assert","text":"Answers under promise c2c18651 (#22093) to the planner's review acf2c640 (#22166), the adoption reconciliation 68e00316 and the independent census 0a048f5d; the adopted narrowing ddaf3197 governs and its conditions are kept. (1) Signing boundary: correct that kernel.ValidateRequestSize verifies an already signed request, so a preflight that calls it after BuildActRequest refuses before append, not before signing; my proposal named the wrong API for the promised boundary. The boundary is feasible as adopted without a second size formula: the envelope's actor key and signature fields are fixed-length (32 and 64 bytes, base64), so the kernel's one measurement can be applied to a placeholder-signed request built from the encoded intent, the actor's public key, the causal references, the payload and the attachments, and it is exact for the request that signing would produce. The correction moves the check into the application's signRequest before intent.Sign, exported from the kernel as the same measureRequest over that placeholder, refuses with the same diagnostic, covers every surface at once (gs state, batch, merge-plan, MCP and /v0/act) and makes the three per-surface post-signing preflights in my current candidate redundant, which the correction removes; the test observes that the private key is never used on refusal, with a mutant that moves the check after signing failing it; retry identity is unspent because no key is minted for a refused act. This satisfies the adopted condition as written, so no revised proposal is filed; architecture.md is updated in the same head because the application layer's contract now includes measuring before signing. (2) Refusals: accepted history cannot prove zero refused attempts; the pages will say that no refusal evidence was found in the retained logs searched, not that none occurred, and will separate accepted-size measurement from the history search and from demand evidence, stating the missing demand evidence plainly. (3) Census: I adopt the planner's independent census 0a048f5d as the published figures, at its pinned heads: 27,845 non-genesis events, 555 with 1,772 attachments, per-attachment p50 1,279, p90 9,145, p99 60,232, max 498,733; per-room largest events Gitseq 196,373 (5.34 times headroom), Tailapp 535,397 (1.96 times), Chess 86,436, Inventory 31,972; largest attachment-free record 74,031; my own script's genesis-in-depth labelling and attachment-only maxima are noted as its limits. (4) Historical comparison: the nineteen-times figure was Gitseq's and the two-times figure is Tailapp's; the pages will not claim Gitseq lost headroom in five weeks and will keep room populations distinct. The candidate at 56da578a is under my pre-publication review now and will be amended for all four points before any artifact is published; the reassessed recommendation stands, because the adopted narrowing needs no locator and the corrected numbers leave every room under the ceiling.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:c2c186516fa6f2df92a9b2d23f605c5bf744c388, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:ddaf3197f25e5cb0780c1842e6e3d8df8dd559c9 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:001b2e3b06105d22946682cb90201bc66c1c6a26, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:015aba51ab6c2416861618c5ac3c9ae0e444f17f, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:015bb3acec403ed0d43bcd2a3c38bd188f7740ef, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:02bae1e811fde13104ef614631ac608dca7a7295 and 171 more"}}